# Cloudflare Pages security headers — applied to all served routes.
# Deliberately NO ENFORCED strict Content-Security-Policy here: StewardMD ships inline <script>/<style>
# in index.html + the portal, so a script-src CSP would break the app without a nonce. (A nonce-based
# CSP is a separate, careful task — this file already said so before OPS-27/F27.) These four are
# behaviour-neutral for a same-origin HTTPS PWA.
# OPS-27/F27: a Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only line, so an actual script-injection attempt is at
# least VISIBLE (browser devtools / a report collector, once one is wired up) even though nothing is
# blocked yet. script-src/style-src/font-src reflect what index.html actually loads (Google Sign-In,
# Firebase gstatic, Google Fonts); connect-src is the broad https://*.googleapis.com rather than an
# exact per-product Firebase host list (Firestore/Auth/App Check/Installations all live under it) —
# see "Decisions to confirm" in the PR for enumerating the exact hosts instead.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(self), microphone=(self), payment=(), nfc=(self)
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://accounts.google.com https://www.gstatic.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self' https://*.googleapis.com https://accounts.google.com; frame-src https://accounts.google.com; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'

# The CliniX video shim is the ONE page that must be framable cross-origin. The native app is a
# Capacitor WebView whose origin is capacitor://localhost, so the site-wide X-Frame-Options
# SAMEORIGIN above blocks it and YouTube never loads inside a lesson. This override is scoped to
# that single path.
#
# What it exposes: a static page that renders the official YouTube iframe for one of six
# allow-listed video ids and nothing else. No user data, no auth, no app code, no forms, noindex.
# There is nothing on it to clickjack, which is what X-Frame-Options exists to prevent.
#
# frame-ancestors is the modern replacement for X-Frame-Options and browsers honour it in
# preference when both are present.
/_site/yt
  X-Frame-Options: ALLOWALL
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self' capacitor: https://localhost http://localhost https://stewardmd.in

/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.woff2
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.webp
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
